config AL_SSM
	bool "Annapurna Labs al_ssm crypto/RAID UDMA mem-to-mem test (iodma)"
	depends on AL_ETH
	help
	  Adds the `iodma` command: a mem-to-mem DMA self-test on the Alpine V2
	  SSM crypto/RAID engine (PCI 1c36:0022), which drives a SEPARATE al_udma
	  instance from al_eth's. Probes the endpoint, sets up a RAID-queue UDMA
	  ring in low DRAM, runs an AL_RAID_OP_MEM_CPY copy and verifies it, and
	  dumps the M2S engine state in the same format as al_eth so the two are
	  directly comparable (does THIS UDMA's descriptor read complete where the
	  eth's hangs, #90?).

	  Depends on AL_ETH: reuses that module's compiled udma/iofic HAL objects
	  and the al_unit_adapter_init stub. Only the SSM/RAID/m2m-udma glue is
	  added here. Build/diagnostic feature - no traffic path.
